# Built indexes are reproducible from source by `drf build`, and their
# manifest content_hash is what makes two builds comparable. Committing a
# .db would also commit SQLite's header change counter, which differs between
# byte-identical builds - exactly the fragile comparison this project avoids.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# Generated documentation is deliberately COMMITTED, not ignored. It is
# rendered from spec/ by `drf docs build`, and tests/test_docs.py re-renders
# and compares - so a hand edit fails the suite. An ignored file cannot be
# checked, which would make the whole hand-edit guarantee unenforceable.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
